\import{algorithms-macros}

\title{#{\Theta(n!)}: factorial (inputs up to #{11})}

\p{#{n!} corresponds to the number of distinct orderings of #{n} things. If an algorithm takes #{\Theta(n!)} it is really, really bad. In fact, #{k^n} is #{o(n!)} for all #{k}.}

